Backport of upstream DXMT's `d3d11.defuseFma` option (854aed0 + 4ab5983 + 59bf42f + 43a16e9, 2026-04, on
main after v0.72), reduced to that one option, plus a God of War (2018) profile entry.

Why: v0.72 (3d8d2aa) lowers DXBC `mad` to a FUSED air.fma only when the instruction is `precise` — and marks
EVERY instruction precise in shaders compiled without refactoringAllowed — but to a separate mul + add
otherwise. A depth prepass and the later G-buffer pass can therefore compute SV_Position through different
roundings (fused vs. unfused), so the depth differs by an ulp and the G-buffer's DepthFunc = EQUAL test
fails on scattered pixels: God of War's "white dots" (diagnosed by a Reddit user, 2026: the only EQUAL
depth-stencil state is the G-buffer one, and swapping it to GREATER_EQUAL removes every speck). Upstream
added `defuseFma` for the same class of problem in Shadow of the Tomb Raider; with it on, every fma() is
emitted as mul + add, so both passes round identically. Position is already `air.invariant` and vertex
shaders already have fast-math off, so preserveInvariance-style changes would not help here.

Same option name, config key and flag bit as upstream (bit 0, SAMPLE_NAN_TO_ZERO, is not backported); the
flag is folded into every shader variant digest so the on-disk shader cache keeps fused and defused
variants apart. Override per launch with DXMT_CONFIG="d3d11.defuseFma=False" (user config wins over the
profile). Drop this patch once DXMT_VERSION includes upstream 43a16e9 — but keep the GoW.exe profile by
re-adding it (or upstreaming it) if the fix is confirmed on device.

